  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. It moved the clamped value the wrong way when a bound was open (`min_open` or `max_open`).\n\nThe method returned `bound - dir`, but `dir` is already the direction pointing back into the valid range (+1 from a minimum, -1 from a maximum). Clamping to an open minimum of 0 therefore gave -1, which is out of range. It now returns `bound + dir`, so the same case gives 1.\n\nThe existing tests in `tests/test_types.py` pass (41 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't add a test for the open-bound clamping case.",
